! mcp_bootstrap_p83.strap -- MCP INITIALIZATION, printed page 83:
! the MOVE routine's constants, its index-register names, and the
! SAVE AND RESTORE AREA FOR INDEXES.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.90, header "PAGE NUMBER 83".
! docs/transcription_workflow.md has the loop this was transcribed by.
!
! CONTIGUOUS WITH printed p.80 BY ADDRESS.  p.80's last line is 31,
! "B,1.00($15)" at 004627.00 -- ASSIGN's return -- and this page's
! first located line is 7, at 004627.40, the very next half word.
! printed pp.81 and 82 compile NOTHING (their LOCATION columns are
! empty down the whole page), which is why the two pages between them
! leave no gap.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS, every one recovered from this page's own binary output
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! A SYN card prints its VALUE in the location column, so the five
! SYNs to symbols this project has not read yet give those symbols'
! addresses directly:
!
!   line 15  T LIMB  SYN,SBAPP    prints 002155.00  -> S BAPP  = 2155.0
!   line 16  T SYRFT SYN,SSYRFT   prints 002157.40  -> S SYRFT = 2157.40
!   line 17  T BAMCP SYN,SMAXUB   prints 002153.00  -> S MAXUB = 2153.0
!   line 18  T MAXRF SYN,SMAXRN   prints 002155.40  -> S MAXRN = 2155.40
!   line 19  T MARK  SYN,SMARK    prints 002162.40  -> S MARK  = 2162.40
!
! S MAXUB AT 2153.0 AGREES WITH TWO PAGES ALREADY TRANSCRIBED:
! docs/NEXT.md records printed p.40 and p.28 both placing S MAXUB and
! S BA MCP at (8)2153.0, and printed p.98 line 33's "S MAXUB SYN,
! S BA MCP" says they are the same symbol.  Three sources, one value.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE INDEX NAMES, AND ONE OF THEM IS A CHAINED SYN
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Lines 21-33 name $1-$12 for the MOVE routine, and the LOCATION
! column prints each one's WORD: "T MX1 SYN,$1" prints 000021.00,
! and 0o21 = 17, which is X1 (X0-X15 occupy words 16-31).  "T MLXA
! SYN,$12" prints 000034.00 = word 28 = X12.  The page confirms the
! register-to-word mapping on its own.
!
! >>> LINE 32 IS "T MXH SYN,T MX1" -- A SYN WHOSE TARGET IS ITSELF A
! SYN OF $1 -- AND IT PRINTS 000021.00, TMX1's OWN WORD. <<<  That is
! the construct strap_asm.py recorded only one level deep until
! 2026-10-30, which made "LX,TIXF,TCHSXW" on printed p.72 compile with
! j=0 and cost the boot sixteen million steps.  tests/
! verify_syn_chain_reg.py pins the fix; this page is the next user of
! it, and its printed value is the independent check.
!
! >>> IN ENTRY MODE THE SPACE AFTER THE COMMA IS DATA. <<<
! The first draft wrote "(AX)DD(BU,24,6), IOD X" with a space, as the
! rest of this deck's operands are written, and every symbol after it
! landed six bits late -- T MREEL at 004630.52 where the page prints
! 004630.44.  Measured directly:
!
!     '(AX)DD(BU,24,6), IOD X'  -> 30 bits
!     '(AX)DD(BU,24,6),IOD X'   -> 24 bits
!
! and 24 is the declared length.  The trailing X is the terminator the
! assembler requires ("entry-mode datum is not terminated by 'X'"), not
! a character of the datum.  T M6BL's operand is SEVEN BLANKS and the X,
! which is how a 48-bit field of 6-bit blanks is written.

SBAPP   SYN, (8)2155.0
SSYRFT  SYN, (8)2157.40
SMAXUB  SYN, (8)2153.0
SMAXRN  SYN, (8)2155.40
SMARK   SYN, (8)2162.40

        SLC, (8)4627.40

        CNOP                         ! line 7
TMMAX   DD(BU,12), 4095              ! line 8  -THE VERY MAX DISK REF
TMIOD   (AX)DD(BU,24,6),IOD X       ! line 9  - BCD CODE FOR IOD
TMREEL  (AX)DD(BU,24,6),REELX       ! line 10 -BCD CODE FOR A REEL
TLBL    (AX)DD(BU,6,6),LX           ! line 11 -LABELED CHARACTER
TNCP    (AX)DD(BU,6,6),NX           ! line 12 -NOT PROTECT CHARACTER
TM6BL   (AX)DD(BU,48,6),       X           ! line 13
TERFLG  VF, 0                        ! line 14 -IOD CARD ERROR INDICATOR
TLIMB   SYN, SBAPP                   ! line 15 -UPPER BOUNDARY
TSYRFT  SYN, SSYRFT                  ! line 16 -THE ADDRESS OF THE ...
TBAMCP  SYN, SMAXUB                  ! line 17 -FOR CHECKING THE UPPER ...
TMAXRF  SYN, SMAXRN                  ! line 18 -THE MAX REF NO. PER ...
TMARK   SYN, SMARK                   ! line 19 -THE NEXT VACANT REEL ...
TMX1    SYN, $1                      ! line 21
TMXA    SYN, $2                      ! line 22 -PP REF WORD LOCATOR
TMXB    SYN, $3                      ! line 23 -I/O REQ TABLE PICK ...
TMXC    SYN, $4                      ! line 24 -SYMB I/O TABLE INDEX
TMXD    SYN, $5                      ! line 25 -FILE AREA TABLE INDEX
TMXE    SYN, $6                      ! line 26 -UNIT AREA TABLE INDEX
TMXF    SYN, $7                      ! line 27 -REEL POOL INDEX
TMXG    SYN, $8                      ! line 28 -TEMPORARY INDEX
TMXEE   SYN, $9                      ! line 29 -TEMPORARY INDEX
TMXI    SYN, $10                     ! line 30 -CONTROL WORD INDEX
TMXGA   SYN, $11                     ! line 31 -TEMPORARY INDEX
TMXH    SYN, TMX1                    ! line 32
TMLXA   SYN, $12                     ! line 33 -CONVERSION ROUTINE

! ---- SAVE AND RESTORE AREA FOR INDEXES ---------------------------
        CNOP                         ! line 39
TSIOXW  DRZ(BU,64), (15)             ! line 40
TDKSAV  VF, 0                        ! line 42 -ADDRESS OF THE UNIT ...

